fix(ui): the LAYERS control now lists what the user can actually switch

It was a vertical-layer list wearing the name of a layer control. Measured in
the DOM: in overview it was `hidden` with 0 rows, and turning 風場 on from the
rail left the panel still showing only 停水受影響地區. So a user who switched a
layer on from the rail had no way to see it, or switch it off, from the map's
own control.

It now carries BOTH kinds of row — the active vertical's own layers, and the
rail's toggles — in every mode.

The important part is that there is ONE implementation of "on". A rail-backed
row CLICKS the rail's own button rather than setting aria-pressed and calling
toggleLayer directly: doing the latter bypasses the button's onclick, so the
button's next-click calculation (`next = aria-pressed !== "true"`) then computes
the opposite of what the user expects. Measured: clicking the row turned the
wind layer on, and the next click on the rail button turned it on again instead
of off — which is why wind reported 0 features inside the harness while working
perfectly in isolation. The button owns the state; both controls press it.

Also removed the `hidden` branch in setRows([]), which was what made the control
disappear entirely in overview.

Four harness checks were reading `querySourceFeatures`, which only returns
features in tiles loaded for the CURRENT viewport (Pitfall 7 — the same trap as
the aircraft check fixed in the previous commit). By that point in the run the
map has been resized and panned, so wind reported 0 barbs while its source held
8 and its toggle was correctly pressed. Aircraft, wind, stations and the water
districts now all read the source GeoJSON, and the wind diagnostic reports the
toggle state and source count on failure so the next person is not left
guessing which of the three layers of the stack broke.

Harness 61 -> 63 checks, green twice.

Refs: WORK_ORDER.md §2.2, AGENTS.md Pitfall 7 and Pitfall 14
